VNU initial ramdisk

This tree is packed into initrd.tar and handed to the kernel by the
boot loader as a Multiboot2 module. The kernel unpacks it into /initrd
of the RAM filesystem at boot, so a file can be added to the running
system by dropping it here and rebuilding the image - no change to the
kernel is needed.

Everything under this directory arrives at /initrd/<name> in the guest.
